# Assignment 6 is an A6-only upload (user, 2026-11-07): the full game lives
# here on disk so it runs, but git tracks only what the assignment asks for.
# Everything is ignored by default. The game files a reviewer needs to open and
# run the project (scripts/a6_tracked_files.py: the export whitelist, its
# .import/.uid sidecars, tests/ and scripts/) are added explicitly with
# `git add -f`; A6's own new paths are listed back in below.
/*
!/.gitignore
!/.gitattributes
!/*.md
!/scripts/
!/effects/
!/previews/
!/captures/
!/prompts/
!/sessions/
!/evidence/
!/youtube/
# Game files A6 reads or changes (their starting version is committed first)
!/project.godot
!/shaders/
/shaders/*
!/shaders/particles_generated.gdshader*
!/tests/
!/tests/**
/tests/**/*.log
# Cited logs only
!/logs/
/logs/*
!/logs/baseline-*/
/logs/baseline-*/*
!/logs/baseline-*/summary.txt
!/logs/*hit_burst*.log
!/logs/*fire_pit*.log
!/logs/cost_effects*.log
# Film media never goes to GitHub
*.mp4
*.mp3
*.wav
*.mov
.godot/
